# oracle: dynamical_matrix regular on the same 8-atom perturbed LJ cell (delta 1e-2): the matrix file, and the final forces, which native leaves as those of the last displaced evaluation
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo none, atoms 3.3e-16; the matrix file agrees within 1e-10. Without keeping the last displaced forces (the engine recomputed them at the restored positions) atom 4 fz was 0.0140 instead of native 0.0263.
# oracle-files: w241to_dynmat_lj.dat
# oracle-compare: thermo=none atoms=all filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify    map array
lattice         none 1.0
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 single 0.10 0.05 0.02 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.05 0.12 0.08 units box
create_atoms    1 single 0.07 2.11 0.15 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.02 2.06 0.11 units box
create_atoms    1 single 0.13 0.09 2.07 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.09 0.04 2.13 units box
create_atoms    1 single 0.06 2.14 2.04 units box
create_atoms    1 single 2.11 2.09 2.10 units box
mass            1 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
neighbor        0.3 bin
dynamical_matrix all regular 0.01 file w241to_dynmat_lj.dat
